  ],
  "meaning": "due = the age the dose is given from. until = the last day it is on time. A dose not given after the 'until' age is overdue. DEFAULT RULES (clinic decisions, not part of the national table): infant doses (birth, 6, 10, 14 weeks) are overdue 4 weeks after the due age; a dose given in a window (9-12 months, 16-24 months) is overdue after the window ends; later single-age doses (5-6 years, 10 and 16 years) are overdue after the stated range or one year.",
